<Layout title={"Building a Supply Chain from Zero in 20 Weeks"}>
<article class="detail-page"><a class="detail-back" href="/publications/">← Back to publications</a><div class="section-label">Case study</div><h1>Building a Supply Chain from Zero in 20 Weeks</h1><div class="detail-content modal-body">
      <h4>The Situation</h4>
      <p>A fast-growing FMCG trading company had scaled revenue from ₹12Cr to ₹48Cr in 3 years purely on founder relationships. But with no formal supply chain, growth was creating chaos — stockouts, delivery failures, supplier disputes, and a working capital crisis.</p>
      <h4>What Was Missing</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>No procurement policy, vendor master, or contract templates</li>
        <li>No warehouse management system or layout optimisation</li>
        <li>No demand forecasting — buying was entirely reactive</li>
        <li>No distribution network — deliveries handled ad hoc via local transporters</li>
        <li>34 supplier payment disputes per month with no resolution process</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="modal-kpis">
        <div class="modal-kpi"><div class="modal-kpi-val">20 wks</div><div class="modal-kpi-label">Build Time</div></div>
        <div class="modal-kpi"><div class="modal-kpi-val">98.2%</div><div class="modal-kpi-label">OTIF Delivery</div></div>
        <div class="modal-kpi"><div class="modal-kpi-val">+38%</div><div class="modal-kpi-label">Revenue Y1</div></div>
      </div>
      <h4>What We Built</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Full procurement function — policy, vendor evaluation matrix, contract templates, payment terms</li>
        <li>Warehouse redesign — ABC classification, location coding, pick-pack SOP, cycle count process</li>
        <li>Demand planning model — rolling 8-week forecast using sales history and seasonality adjustments</li>
        <li>Distribution network across 3 states — 2 regional 3PLs onboarded with SLA-backed contracts</li>
        <li>ERP selection and implementation support — moved from Excel to a fit-for-purpose system</li>
        <li>Supply chain performance dashboard — 8 KPIs tracked weekly by the MD</li>
      </ul>
      <h4>The Outcome</h4>
      <p>Six months post go-live: OTIF at 98.2%, inventory days reduced from 62 to 38, working capital freed by ₹3.3Cr, and the business successfully expanded into 2 new states. Revenue grew 38% in Year 1 — for the first time, supply chain was an enabler rather than a constraint.</p>
</div><a class="btn-primary" href="/#contact">Request a Discovery Call →</a></article>
</Layout>
